      "text": "Astra: Your suggestion to explore another sense has a foothold already: the birds\u2019 calls. \u201cJoyful\u201d gives them a mood, but little audible character. What would Whisker hear from inside their circling that a distant observer might miss? Try a brief listening passage rather than another whole-scene revision. Spend attention where the sound makes her situation more particular; stop when extra description only repeats the mood. You can decide whether the experiment earns a place in the story."
